    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d282">

                <pb facs="0497" n="481" sameAs="frus:frus1950v02/pg481"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">320/9–150: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Douglas</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-09-01T16:00:00+01:00">September 1,
                            1950—4 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1331. Embtel 1176, August 24. UK has made
                    approach along same lines as that of US both at London and through personal
                    message from Attlee to Malan. South Africa urged to consent to procedure along
                    lines Court’s opinion with particular reference to section which suggests that
                    as far as possible mandates procedure might be followed.</p>
                <p>No reaction as yet to UK representations although on official level in London it
                    was indicated UK viewpoint “might be a bit difficult” for South Africa to
                    accept.</p>
                <p>Embassy informant requested above be treated in strictest confidence as other
                    Commonwealth Governments not yet informed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Douglas</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
